{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/308284-using-the-father-wolf-myth","id":308284,"title":"Using the Father Wolf myth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-10T09:36:50-08:00","id":308284,"title":"Using the Father Wolf myth","content":"The point of the Father Wolf myth is that it in part is what answers the question &quot;What do werewolves do?&quot;, yes? The story of Father Wolf gives you one possible answer. You read this tale of a primal ancestor who tried to keep his territory under control, and it gives you a potential structure to follow. Structure's good in a game, because it's giving you default story ideas that come easily to Storytellers. In this case, it's recreating Father Wolf's spirit hunts, and dealing with werewolves who also believe in this myth and hate you for the part your ancestors played in it. <br /> <br /> The Father Wolf myth is also big on symbolism; a story of personal responsibility \u2014 of a pack of werewolves making a terrible decision that nonetheless had to be made, mirroring possible situations and outcomes in the lives of many Forsaken packs. In the World of Darkness, doing the right thing means that you're going to suffer, and this is reflected well in the Father Wolf myth. You have this flawed paradise that threatened to consume the world, and thus, had to be brought down; and you have the cowards and fools who just didn't have the guts to act when necessity arose, and, due to their own moral failings, now seek to purge those who did the right thing from the face of the earth. <br /> <br /> So - how have you used this stuff in the context of your games? What sort of role does the myth play in your games? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T14:07:10-08:00","id":308502,"title":"","content":"Barring the occasional Fire-Touched zealot quoting verses of the Fall, none so much. My games are way too focused in the here and now to prominently feature baseless myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T14:52:44-08:00","id":308528,"title":"","content":"Outside of certain ceremonies and the rivalry between the Pure and the Forsaken it didn't really come up much. Between him being dead for however long and lack of real presence in the modern world, coupled with the alternatives myths that, at least in some cases, seem more likely, we've found it hard to fit the legend into the here and now.<br /> <br /> That said, in one game, the Firstborn had a big presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2014, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}